428.html\"},{\"title\":\"Nvidia smashes Q4 2026 with $68 billion in revenue, and a Q1 outlook that quashes AI bubble talk | Fortune\",\"url\":\"https://fortune.com/2026/02/25/nvidia-nvda-earnings-q4-results-jensen-huang/\"},{\"title\":\"Nvidia Posts Record Q4 Revenue of $68.1B and Fiscal 2026 Sales of $215.9B as AI Demand Accelerates\",\"url\":\"https://www.masdark.com/15585\"},{\"title\":\"NVIDIA Corporation - NVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Fourth Quarter and Fiscal 2026\",\"url\":\"https://investor.nvidia.com/news/press-release-details/2026/NVIDIA-Announces-Financial-Results-for-Fourth-Quarter-and-Fiscal-2026/default.aspx\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here is the information about NVIDIA's Q4 2026 financial metrics:\n\n## Q4 2026 Actual Results:\n\n**Gross Margins:**\nFor the quarter, GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins were 75.0% and 75.2%, respectively.\n\n**Operating Margin:**\nThe search results do not contain specific operating margin figures for Q4 2026.\n\n**Stock-Based Compensation (SBC):**\nGAAP and non-GAAP gross margins are expected to be 74.9% and 75.0%, respectively, plus or minus 50 basis points, inclusive of a 0.1% impact from stock-based compensation expense. This represents the impact of SBC on Q1 FY27 guidance, though the gross margin guidance for the quarter itself does not break out a separate SBC impact beyond the 0.1% shown.\n\n## Q1 FY27 Guidance:\n\n**Gross Margins:**\nGAAP and non-GAAP gross margins are expected to be 74.9% and 75.0%, respectively, plus or minus 50 basis points, inclusive of a 0.1% impact from stock-based compensation expense.\n\n**Operating Expenses & SBC:**\nGAAP and non-GAAP operating expenses are expected to be approximately $7.7 billion and $7.5 billion, respectively, inclusive of $1.9 billion of stock-based compensation expense.\n\n**Important Note on SBC Accounting Change:**\nBeginning in the first quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA will include stock-based compensation expense in non-GAAP financial measures.\